bss-transition-handling

Moving the peer lists per-radio also moved the radio lookup for the HTT peer
map/unmap events out to the T2H handler, where it lost its NULL check.
ath11k_mac_get_ar_by_vdev_id() returns NULL once ath11k_core_halt() has cleared
allocated_vdev_map and pdevs_active, and the T2H receive path keeps running
then, so a peer unmap reaped afterwards dereferences NULL in softirq. Check it
at all four call sites and drop the "&& ar" left behind in peer.c, where ar is
now dereferenced on entry.

The peer_free path in ath11k_peer_map_v2_event() unlocked base_lock a second
time on the way out through exit:, and reached ath11k_peer_delete(), which
takes a mutex and waits for a completion, from that same softirq. Unwind the
peer that was just allocated and listed instead; ath11k_peer_create() then
times out and the association is rejected.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>

